getColumnNo [SimTalk]
Searches for the column which contains a user-defined column index of the DataTable designated by
<Path>.
Remarks
Note
If the table contains a large number of entries, you might want to activate Fast Index Access.
The method only works for simple data types, such as string, integer, etc.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.getColumnNo(ColumnIndex:any) → integer
Parameter
The parameter ColumnIndex of data type any designates the column index which Plant Simulation
searches for.
Return Value
The return value has the data type integer.
Is the column number.
Is -1 if the column index does not exist.
Example
var column : integer
column := MyDataTable.getColumnNo("Urgent")
SimTalk
