appendRow [SimTalk]
Adds a new row to the DataTable designated by <Path> and writes the passed values to the individual
columns.
Remarks
If the row has a row index, Plant Simulation writes the first value into the row index.
You cannot add a row if the maximum number of rows has already been reached.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.appendRow(Value:any[, Value:any, ..., Value:any]) -> integer
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Value of data type any designates the value that Plant Simulation is to write to the first
cell in the first free row.
• The optional parameters Value of data type any designate additional values that Plant Simulation is to
write to the remaining cells in the first free row.
Return Value
The return value has the data type integer. It is the index of the appended row.
Example
