copyFilteredTableTo [SimTalk]
Copies all rows of the source table designated by <Path> into the target table for which the Condition
returns true.
Remarks
copyFilteredTableTo also copies the column index if you defined it.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.copyFilteredTableTo(TargetTable:table, Condition:string)
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter TargetTable of data type table designates the target table into which the rows of the
source table will be copied.
• The parameter Condition of data type string designates the condition.
Within the condition the anonymous identifier @ references the DataTable and the variable ySelf
contains the row number of the row that is to be copied.
If the Condition returns true, the row of the source table is going to be copied to the target table.
Example
DataTable.copyFilteredTableTo(DataTable1, "@[2, ySelf] = 3")
copyFilteredTableTo [SimTalk]
11-4164 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

copyRangeTo [SimTalk]
Copies the designated range of the source table designated by <Path> into the target table.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.copyRangeTo(SourceRange:listrange, TargetTable:any, 
TargetColumn:any, TargetRow:any)
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter SourceRange of data type listrange designates the range to be copied.
• The parameter TargetTable of data type any designates the target table.
• The parameter TargetColumn of data type any designates the column in the target table, where Plant
Simulation inserts the copied range.
• The parameter TargetRow of data type any designates the row in the target table, where Plant
Simulation inserts the copied range.
Example
tableA.copyRangeTo({2,2}..{*,*}, tableB, 1,1)
Depending if Column Index Belongs to Contents is active or not, the range has different effects on the
method copyRangeTo of the DataTable.
tableA.copyRangeTo({2,*}, tableB, 1,1)
• If tableA has a column index and the column index belongs to the contents, the entire contents of
column 2 is copied to the designated target DataTable, including the column index.
• If tableB has a column index and the column index does not belong to the contents, only the contents
of the column is copied, excluding the column index.
See also
Specifying a Range of Cells [several columns] > Column Index Belongs to Contents
copyRangeTo [SimTalk]
