determineRange [SimTalk] - DataTable
Resolves the actual list range for the DataTable designated by <Path>.
Remarks
The method determineRange assigns the boundaries of the list range to the local variables, which you
specify.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.determineRange(Range:listrange, byRef StartColumn:integer, byRef 
StartRow:integer, byRef EndColumn:integer, byRef EndRow:integer)
Local Variables
You can specify the following local variables:
• The parameter Range of data type listrange designates the range of the DataTable.
• The local variable StartColumn of data type integer designates the number of the first column.
• The local variable StartRow of data type integer designates the number of the first row.
• The local variable EndColumn of data type integer designates the number of the last column.
• The local variable EndRow of data type integer designates the number of the last row.
Example
param a: any
var fromX, fromY, toX, toY: integer
if isListRange(a) 
   MyDataTable.determineRange(a, fromX, fromY, toX, toY)
   print "{",fromX,",",fromY,"}..{",toX,",",toY,"}"
end
// You can call this method like this: 
myMethod({2,3})
myMethod({1,1}..{2,*})
// range with a user-defined column/row index
myMethod({#7,"abc"}..{#8,*})
determineRange [SimTalk] - DataTable
Plant Simulation Help 11-4167
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

See also
