mergeTable [SimTalk]
Copies the columns of the source table to the target table designated by <Path>.
Remarks
The method mergeTable uses the row index to correctly assign the rows. For this reason both DataTables
have to have a row index otherwise the method will not copy anything.
The method searches for the index of each row in the source table in the target table. If it exists, it adds
the column values of the source table to the target table.
If the source table contains a great number of rows, we recommend activating Fast Index Access as all
index entries of the target table have to be found in the source table.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.mergeTable(SourceTable:table)
Parameters
The parameter SourceTable of data type table designates the source table whose rows will be copied to the
target table.
Example
TargetTable.mergeTable(SourceTable)
Compare this example.
mergeTable [SimTalk]
