setCommonFormatData [SimTalk] - DataTable
Sets the common format data for the subtables contained in columns of data type list/table of the target
DataTable designated by <Path> for which you activated Common Format for the specified column.
Remarks
If you activated Common Format for a column, assigning a subtable to a table cell creates a copy of the
assigned table. Otherwise Plant Simulation enters a reference to the assigned table. The reason for this is
that it does not make sense to enter a reference if Common Format is active as the assigned table should
not be subject to the common format.
setCommonFormatData applies to the DataTable and the TimeSequence.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.setCommonFormatData(FormatData:table[, Column:any])
<Path>.setCommonFormatData(FormatData:list[, Column:any])
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter FormatData of data type table designates the table which contains the desired
formatting for the subtables.
The parameter FormatData of data type list designates the list which contains the desired formatting for
the sublists.
• The optional parameter Column of data type any designates the column of the table designated by
<Path>. The column has to be of data type list/table and Common Format has to be activated. If you do
not specify this parameter, the common format data will be set for the first column.
Example
MyTargetTable.setCommonFormatData(DataTable,2)
SimTalk
