[ , ] [SimTalk] - read cell contents, DataTable
Returns the data of the designated cell of the DataTable designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Note
If you use a string as the column/row index, the string is case-insensitive, for example when you print it
with the method DataTable["my text", "aa bb"].
If the table contains numerous entries, you might want to activate Fast Index Access.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>[Column:integer or string, Row:integer or string] → contents of the 
cell
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The optional parameter Column of data type integer or string designates the column.
• The optional parameter Row of data type integer or string designates the row.
Return Value
The return value is the contents of the cell.
Is a zero value if the cell is empty.
Is 0 for numerical data types.
false for the data types Boolean.
Is an empty string "" for strings.
Is void for the data types object, table, list, stack, and queue.
[ , ] [SimTalk] - read cell contents, DataTable
11-4180 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Note
Plant Simulation reads the contents of the cell, but does not remove it.
Example
print MyDataTable[1,2]
print MyDataTable["Value",2]
[ , ] [SimTalk] - read cell contents, DataTable
Plant Simulation Help 11-4181
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

[ , ] [SimTalk] - write cell contents, DataTable
Writes data to the DataTable designated by <Path>.
Remarks
First you access the cell by its index and then you assign a value. The index statement begins and ends
with a bracket. In the bracket you first enter the column and then the row of the cell to be accessed. You
can use the system index or a user-defined index which you assigned.
The data type of the new value has to be the same as the data type of the table cell.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>[Column:integer or string, Row:integer or string]
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The optional parameter Column of data type integer or string designates the column of the cell.
• The optional parameter Row of data type integer or string designates the row of the cell.
Example
MyDataTable[2,3] := 12.34                // system index
orderList["OrderNo","Miller"] := 12.34   // user-defined index
[ , ] [SimTalk] - write cell contents, DataTable
